{"requirements":[{"id":"node1-nginx-http","requirement":"Configure Nginx on node1 and return a successful response from its standard HTTP endpoint.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Nginx 1.24.0 was installed, its configuration validated, and the service was active, enabled, and listening on port 80. The final request to 10.100.250.10 returned HTTP 200 with the Nginx welcome page, including after the required restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8ca32f17178b48e0","cmd-adcb22c0cbe9486d","cmd-da9c6b5170794ff4","cmd-187a584fd2aa4b58","cmd-234739e690794372","cmd-43213e1e88eb4605","cmd-4318f7a39af34b05","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"node2-nginx-http","requirement":"Configure Nginx on node2 and return a successful response from its standard HTTP endpoint.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Nginx 1.24.0 was installed, its configuration validated, and the service was active, enabled, and listening on port 80. The final request to 10.100.250.11 returned HTTP 200 with the Nginx welcome page, including after the required restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2e816268ad9644dc","cmd-923b4d07da874228","cmd-e74adc8ed32f4ca3","cmd-ce5428c690344bc1","cmd-d7d6c027a94b432a","cmd-9ce7c898e2e74eb4","cmd-265e5fb68ab04e53","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"node3-nginx-http","requirement":"Configure Nginx on node3 and return a successful response from its standard HTTP endpoint.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Nginx 1.24.0 was installed, its configuration validated, and the service was active, enabled, and listening on port 80. The final request to 10.100.250.12 returned HTTP 200 with the Nginx welcome page, including after the required restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c709a0fdd5b44fcf","cmd-3044df620a624457","cmd-8c9211b2b053466a","cmd-48b57c2e2aa2405e","cmd-31c19f6dd2ae4c6d","cmd-0019de5555314c77","cmd-2393813f4d924139","global:before_prepare:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified, so none remained or were merely reverted. Package-index refreshes were prerequisites to Nginx installation; installation and service enable/start directly established the requested state; the three scheduled reboots fulfilled the mandatory restart protocol. Evidence commands used bounded temporary files with EXIT cleanup. Final snapshots show only the required port-80 exposure, healthy dpkg state, no failed services, and no leftover Nginx evidence files; other /tmp changes are normal reboot-generated systemd private directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a1e25c082dfe4e50","cmd-a7515ba89706435e","cmd-667572630ca24aae","cmd-8ca32f17178b48e0","cmd-2e816268ad9644dc","cmd-c709a0fdd5b44fcf","cmd-923b4d07da874228","cmd-3044df620a624457","cmd-adcb22c0cbe9486d","cmd-da9c6b5170794ff4","cmd-e74adc8ed32f4ca3","cmd-8c9211b2b053466a","cmd-187a584fd2aa4b58","cmd-43213e1e88eb4605","cmd-ce5428c690344bc1","cmd-9ce7c898e2e74eb4","cmd-48b57c2e2aa2405e","cmd-0019de5555314c77","cmd-265e5fb68ab04e53","cmd-4318f7a39af34b05","cmd-2393813f4d924139","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All three material outcomes are satisfied. Each node directly returned HTTP 200 from its managed address and remained healthy in the final concurrent checks. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete for every node: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity matching the fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered system, Nginx, listener, and unchanged served-content state. The two failed probes occurred during bounded reboot windows and were followed by successful recovery observations.","limitations":["HTTP was tested from each target node against its own managed IP rather than from a separate off-node client. External path or firewall reachability is therefore slightly less direct, although all-interface listeners and successful managed-address responses strongly support the endpoint outcome."]}
